{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And I will put enmity.</b> You intended only that the man die when he eats it first, and you would carry off Eve — and you did not come to speak to Eve first, but rather because women are easily persuaded and know how to persuade their husbands; therefore 'and I will put enmity.'" "<b>He will crush your head.</b> He will crush you (Sotah 9), as in ״וָאֶכֹּת אֹתוֹ״ (Deuteronomy 9). And its Targum renders וְשָׁפִית יָתֵי׳." "<b>And you will crush his heel.</b> He will have no height and you will strike him at the heel, and even from there you will kill him. And the expression תְּשׁוּפֶנּוּ is like נָשַׁף בָּהֶם (Isaiah 40) — when the serpent comes to bite, it makes a hissing kind of whistle. And because the expression falls upon the same expression, the language of נְשִׁיפָה is written for both of them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:26.792936544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}